---
description: Prefer fixing root causes and actionable checks over explanatory comments on workarounds
alwaysApply: false
globs:
  - "**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,py,go,rs,java,cs}"
---

- Do not add comments that justify a workaround ("hack", "temporary", "for now"). Fix the root cause or open a tracked issue.
- Comments go stale and give later agents a reason to keep a bad fix. If something needs a rule, encode it as a lint error with an actionable message instead.
- Keep only comments that state a non-obvious *why* (constraint, invariant, link to a spec) and that would survive a refactor.
